  "description": "OpenAI-SDK-shaped .NET client for Einkr's OpenAI-compatible endpoint (EinkrAIClient.CompleteChat)\n\t\t\t-- for external tools that need a stateless system+user -> text completion without pulling in\n\t\t\tthe rest of Einkr. Talks to the standard POST /v1/chat/completions and GET /v1/models\n\t\t\t(the same endpoints any OpenAI client uses), authenticated with a per-user Einkr API key as a\n\t\t\tBearer token. Single request/response -- no streaming. Depends only on the BCL.\n\n\t\t\t2.0.0 retargets from Einkr's own /api/completions to the OpenAI-compatible /v1 surface;\n\t\t\tModelInfo now carries the OpenAI model id (a string) rather than a numeric id.\n\n\t\t\t2.1.0 adds responseFormat (ChatResponseFormat.CreateJsonObjectFormat / CreateJsonSchemaFormat)\n\t\t\tto request JSON output. CompleteChatAsync gains it before the CancellationToken parameter, so a\n\t\t\tcaller passing the token positionally should pass it by name.\n\n\t\t\t2.2.0 adds image input: new UserChatMessage(text, [new ChatImage(bytes, \"image/webp\")]) sends the\n\t\t\timages inline (base64 data URI) for vision-capable models.",
